{"term":"permanently","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:e92508fd9865d358dd","definition":"In a permanent manner; lastingly.","example":"We made an odd party before the arrival of the Ten, particularly when the Celebrity dropped in for lunch or dinner. He could not be induced to remain permanently at Mohair because Miss Trevor was at Asquith, but he appropriated a Hempstead cart from the Mohair stables and made the trip sometimes twice in a day.","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["temporarily","transiently"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["nonpermanently","permafrozen","semipermanently"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permanently#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:a273ebda155a1eaf22","definition":"Forever.","example":"Necromancers were thought to have the power of restoring activity to the dead, either temporarily or permanently[.]","pos":"adv","synonyms":[],"antonyms":["temporarily","transiently"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["nonpermanently","permafrozen","semipermanently"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/permanently#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ˈpɜː.mə.nənt.li/","us":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/7/7a/En-us-permanently.ogg/En-us-permanently.ogg.mp3"},"wordFamily":["nonpermanently","permafrozen","semipermanently"]}